# Direct Anonymous Attestation, signing phase, random base.
#
#   Vr -> Pr : nV
#   Pr -> Vr : zk_DAA( f, sig_I(f), r | zeta, nym(zeta, f), I, nV )
#
# The platform Pr holds a secret f and a credential sig_I(f) from the issuer.
# Statement DAA: the second hidden component is the issuer's signature on the
# first one, and the second public component is the pseudonym of the first
# hidden component under the base given as first public component.
# The verifier parses the hidden credential with a signer variable of its own
# (DY) and then runs the verification test `ver`.

protocol DAA
roles   Vr Pr
names   Iss DY
nonces  NV NZ NRn
keys    KF
statement DAA : W1 = sig(P2, W0) & P1 = nym(P0, W0)

Vr -> Pr : NV                                                         ; new NV
Pr -> Vr : zk_DAA(KF, sig(Iss, KF), NRn | NZ, nym(NZ, KF), Iss, NV)   ; new NZ, NRn ; recv_as zk_DAA(KF, sig(DY, KF), NRn | NZ, nym(NZ, KF), Iss, NV) ; recv_post ver
